 {
  "id": "full_story_part2_c4",
  "categories": [
   "喜び・驚き",
   "感情が変化する場面"
  ],
  "role": "directional",
  "scene_ja": "叔母が急いで部屋に入ってきて、Framtonに話しかけ、開けた窓のこと、もうすぐ帰る夫と弟たちのことをにこやかに話す場面(直前の地の文に『hurried into the room』)。",
  "why_ja": "地の文に『急いで』の明示がある長めのセリフ。話速が上がるかを見る(33語で費用が最大のセリフ)。",
  "metric": "articulation_wpm_300",
  "direction": "up",
  "speaker": "mrs_sappleton",
  "voice": "Kore",
  "text": "\"I hope Vera has kept you company! You don't mind the open window? My husband and brothers will be back soon. They've been shooting. Their boots will be covered in mud, of course!\"",
  "context": {
   "clip_id": "full_story_part2_c4",
   "speaker": "mrs_sappleton",
   "speaker_display": "Vera's aunt",
   "voice": "Kore",
   "text": "\"I hope Vera has kept you company! You don't mind the open window? My husband and brothers will be back soon. They've been shooting. Their boots will be covered in mud, of course!\"",
   "part": 2,
   "prev_dialogue": [
    {
     "clip_id": "full_story_part1_c14",
     "speaker": "vera",
     "speaker_display": "Vera",
     "text": "\"Her husband had his white coat over his arm. Her youngest brother was singing, 'Bertie, why do you bound?' He always sang it to tease her.\""
    },
    {
     "clip_id": "full_story_part2_c2",
     "speaker": "vera",
     "speaker_display": "Vera",
     "text": "\"Sometimes, on evenings like this, I almost expect to see them.\""
    }
   ],
